    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Let $L=MN.$ What is the value of ${l}_{11}$, if\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,N=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n${l}_{11}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Multiplying the $1$st row in $M$ by the $1$st column in $N$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{l}_{11} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2+6 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
